+# CVE-2026-73089 — False Positive Assessment for browserslist@1.7.7
+
+## Summary
+
+**CVE-2026-73089 does not affect browserslist 1.7.7.**
+The unbounded query-result `cache` / `parseCache` objects in `index.js` were introduced in 4.7.2 (2019-10-22), more than two and a half years after 1.7.7 (2017-03-21). 1.7.7 has no such cache. There is nothing to patch.
+
+---
+
+## CVE Description
+
+Prior to 4.28.7, `index.js` retains every distinct `(queries, context)` result in `cache` and every `parseQueries()` AST in `parseCache` without a size cap, TTL, or eviction. An attacker who can influence repeated `browserslist()` query values (notably `since <year>-<month>-<day>` queries) can generate unbounded distinct cache keys, causing linear memory growth and an out-of-memory crash.
+
+- **CVE ID:** CVE-2026-73089
+- **GHSA:** GHSA-c83g-rgw3-j3cx
+- **CWE:** CWE-770 (Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling)
+- **Severity:** High (CVSS 7.5)
+- **Upstream fix commit:** `f2931a3ff2a3a31abf84ef01a7400b270aad6405` — Fix unbounded memory growth
+- **Fixed version:** 4.28.7
+
+---
+
+## Affected Package
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Ecosystem | npm |
+| Package | browserslist |
+| This version | 1.7.7 |
+| Scanner range | < 4.28.7 (introduced: 0) |
+
+---
+
+## Root Cause of the CVE
+
+```js
+var cache = {}
+var parseCache = {}
+// ...
+if (cache[cacheKey]) return cache[cacheKey]
+cache[cacheKey] = result
+```
+
+The GHSA is explicit that this is **not** `node.js`'s `filenessCache` / `configCache` (filesystem caches). Those are a different subsystem.
+
+---
+
+## Why 1.7.7 Is Not Affected
+
+### 1. The vulnerable cache was introduced almost 3 years after 1.7.7
+
+1.7.7 was tagged 2017-03-21. Commit `2fee1e4` (2019-10-22, first shipped in **4.7.2**) added `var cache = {}` and query-result memoization for the first time in the project's history. `parseCache` arrived still later (4.24.5, commit `1b999cb`). 1.7.7 predates both by years and is part of the pre-rewrite 1.x line (single 648-line `index.js`, backed by `caniuse-db` + `electron-to-chromium`, with no query-caching layer at all).
+
+### 2. Direct code verification
+
+```
+$ git show 1.7.7:index.js | wc -l
+648
+$ git show 1.7.7:index.js | grep -niE "cache|memoiz|CACHE_MAX|boundedCacheSet"
+(no output — zero matches)
+```
+
+The entire file — a single `var browserslist = function (queries, opts) { ... }` closure spanning lines 151–648 — contains no `cache`, `parseCache`, `CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES`, `boundedCacheSet`, or `memoiz` identifier in any form, and no `since <date>` query-parsing logic (the amplification vector cited in the advisory).
+
+### 3. CVE-2026-73088 is a separate issue and is real on 1.7.7
+
+1.7.7 **does** contain the untrusted-stats-ingestion issue fixed by backporting `f9914ad9effc865ccc27d816255625890b31ca51`. That is CVE-2026-73088 and is patched in `patch/CVE-2026-73088/`. This dummy is only for CVE-2026-73089.
+
+### 4. Advisory range is overly broad
+
+OSV lists 1.7.7 because the git event range is `introduced: 0`. The unbounded query cache does not exist until 4.7.2.
+
+---
+
+## Timeline
+
+| Date | Event |
+|---|---|
+| 2017-03-21 | 1.7.7 tagged — no query-result cache in `index.js` |
+| 2019-10-22 | `2fee1e4` adds unbounded `cache` (4.7.2) |
+| 2025-01-08 | `1b999cb` adds `parseCache` (4.24.5) |
+| 2026-07-21 | `f2931a3` converts both to Maps capped at 500 |
+| 2026-08-11 | CVE-2026-73089 published as < 4.28.7 |
+
+---
+
+## Conclusion
+
+**CVE-2026-73089 is a false positive for browserslist@1.7.7.**
+
+No functional source patch is applicable. Scanner findings should be suppressed. (CVE-2026-73088 remains a real backport on this version.)
+
